# Per developer files.
#
# Every one of these is matched with **/ rather than at the root. The plain spellings only
# ever excluded the top level, so a checkout that had been built locally still shipped
# reposilite-frontend/.gradle into the context, and the node-gradle plugin's downloaded
# toolchain in there is a tree of symlinks pointing at host paths that do not exist in the
# image. The build then fails on "Couldn't follow symbolic link", which reads like a broken
# Dockerfile and is really the host leaking in.
**/.idea/
**/.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
.claude/

# The repository history, 124 MB of it, which the build sends to the daemon and then copies
# into a layer on every run. Nothing needs it: the version is a literal in build.gradle.kts
# since Release Please took ownership of it, and the axion-release plugin that used to derive
# it from tags is gone. Leaving it in also means every secret ever committed and reverted is
# present in the build cache.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Dependencies and build output from any module. Without these a host checkout would ship
# its own node_modules into the image, on top of what the build just installed. The two are
# not interchangeable: the images build on alpine, so anything with a native component
# would be the wrong binary for the platform it ends up running on.
**/node_modules/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/dist/

# Dockerfile related files do not need to be included
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.split.yml
.env

# Not used in running application
reposilite-site
reposilite-test
reposilite-plugins
.github/
.codecov.yml
